  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Many variant humans wander without a fixed residence, but inkmen have built a city in Northern Plains that holds three inkman Gu Immortals.",
      "chapters": [
        662
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It is a unique Northern Plains city crowded with inkmen more than humans. The city is a huge mortal Gu House: its houses and city walls shine in a halo of light, then the whole city floats and shrinks.",
      "chapters": [
        1766
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_mortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Lang Ya blessed land, after Lang Ya land spirit blurts the True Yang Building matter, Mo Tan Sang moves first to speak and explains why he is present: inkman city has long had close relations with Lang Ya, his side has some qi path attainment, and he came to help unseal a qi path seal on the land spirit. He adds that Huang Jin tribes jointly suppress inkman city, and that Giant Sun Immortal Venerable once demanded inkman cities offer countless female inkmen as tribute. He invites Fang Yuan to visit inkman city later, and Fang Yuan answers that he will if there is an opportunity.",
      "chapters": [
        662
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "char_mo_tan_sang",
        "fac_lang_ya_sect",
        "fac_huang_jin_bloodline",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan finds Inkman City as a unique Northern Plains city crowded with inkmen more than humans. Mo Tan Sang, still Inkman City Lord and king of the Northern Plains inkmen, is then one of two remaining Gu Immortals of the city. Fang Yuan’s killer move puts the mortals to sleep; the city reveals itself as a huge mortal Gu House, shrinks, and enters his sovereign immortal aperture. The city has over eight hundred thousand people. Mo Tan Sang credits legendary inkman Gu Immortal Yi Yan with creating it, and calls it half an Emperor City beside Central Continent’s Emperor City. Fang Yuan keeps Mo Tan Sang as Inkman City Lord and lands the city in Mini Western Desert inside the aperture.",
      "chapters": [
        1766
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "relocation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_emperor_city",
        "reg_central_continent",
        "loc_mini_western_desert"
      ]
    }
